A||||2||general||Radiator Fan Sender Switch||||1||
Z||000000||general||09-16-2000||10:07 PM||||  On my V-6 fiero my radiator fan recently stopped working.When I turn on the A.C. the fan starts working again.I recently replaced the sender switch,yet the fan does not respond.My question is:On the sender switch are the threads supposed to be coated with teflon or some type of sealer? I know that the temp.switch is not but did'nt know about the fan switch.Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>general '86 SE,V-6,4spd.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-16-2000||10:19 PM||||DO NOT wrap the threads with tape -the sensor shell must be grounded. Also the stock fan doesn't turn on the fan until some foolishly high temp(230 or something)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-16-2000||11:35 PM||||Nope, No tape on fan switch or any of the gauge senders. <P>Yup, turn on is about 235F on the stock type fan switch.<P>You can check the wire to the fan switch by simply grounding it to the block with the key on. Fan should spin right up if it's ok.<BR>||||reg||1
